                <pb facs="0236" n="914" xml:id="pg914"/>


                <head>Copy of form of notification communicated to George F. Seward, Esq., Consul at
                    Shanghai</head>
                <p>I am directed by Anson Burlingame, envoy, &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c., of the
                    United States to China, to give notice that the following revised regulations,
                    opening customhouses at Hankow and Kiukiang, and under which trade is to be
                    carried on, have been communicated to him by the Chinese government, and that
                    they will come into operation on the 1st of January next, at which time they
                    will supersede the provisional regulations of the fifth December, 1861.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>By order of GEORGE F. SEWARD, <hi rendition="#italic">United States
                            Consul, Shanghai.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
